{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d05fdf80c742cec3f5b6e6ac0008fa297b2714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> ordered quadruplets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8c31b328eb3b0252134a4720e161c0fdf641e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1526cb9932bec037165ffee1da1e72935cf3ee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a, b, c, d) = 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce164c229181099582e3d92da175d8a662ad9b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{lcm}(a, b, c, d) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />. What is the smallest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d928edc4d617c71d486dac956c842bddb612ad82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13,860\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 20,790\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 21,560 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 27,720 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 41,580$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"570\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/84497867b1597ebb07b38ddf397ff4938d4566cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\frac{a}{77}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568add7392963d3f6ce25163f6980bdf16fe4d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=\\frac{b}{77}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/112cb6bced22b5ade9768f1fff29969153e7a21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\frac{c}{77}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2bcdc0f1c9deb21d03b5789473007de771133d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\frac{d}{77}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"39\" /> so that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ff841a7b7b7275fd0f78b4bc61c758e2fd499c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gcd(A,B,C,D)=1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\operatorname{lcm}(A,B,C,D) = N = \\frac{n}{77}.\\]\" width=\"433\" height=\"32\" />\nFor each prime power <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6585024dc6db82bcfd717e03212be80536d94a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" /> in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, at least one of the prime factorizations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/37994d1ae8ac92909339d865d551ad53d798fae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B,C,D)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6585024dc6db82bcfd717e03212be80536d94a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" />, at least one has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca495cdbf2b1c55754412b61246a678e8e1726a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, and all must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d736e1e57cbc014d1c0b60eade924e42f92d9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3402c8c30e2c94482c4c650520f63115469dfc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le m\\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81232ecd8d9e4b5c0f24a00dabec238068f26de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tuples of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/87417e9cbbf687a67ad915c542c33623c3d149c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m_1,m_2,m_3,m_4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/13992427c38817d86a2fdee32c4bff1c0aeda9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le m_i\\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/1021079f866261988995f2dd06d08b054ff274cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max{m_i} = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760c14d77b2e7255d33672d96fd686d956860aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min{m_i} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />. Then for the prime factorization <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e1de4d4c5592b26102b9bc3cb92e0b5078906b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=2^{k_2}3^{k_3}5^{k_5}\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65423ff0bf5a26e22df79929b25f80817f2dc96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77000=f(k_2)f(k_3)f(k_5)f(k_7)\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>To derive a formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81232ecd8d9e4b5c0f24a00dabec238068f26de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, we use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Principle_of_Inclusion-Exclusion\" title=\"Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion\">PIE</a>. Let the universal set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> consist of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tuples such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/13992427c38817d86a2fdee32c4bff1c0aeda9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le m_i\\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tuples such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a62965015124fc368d5796c62560bf35f9fe27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max{m_i} \\neq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tuples such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0639c9522691d9c049a7cd6815f9c5dafcdcdc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min{m_i} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796159ab6e186e3675497b6d219b5389ea56175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> choices from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f5186b8dedbb63c34aa8f1cc31a3d11e528b53e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\Omega| = (k+1)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796159ab6e186e3675497b6d219b5389ea56175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> choices from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f022e59a9c13cee43bbc89cfdd865ad45ebec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|X| = k^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796159ab6e186e3675497b6d219b5389ea56175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> choices from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d0390b57cfb65ecac5a27f9258d7ae7af2c7734c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Y| = k^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/7900b13c7d9800367e9ac1f434ab1312b5e43454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X\\cap Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796159ab6e186e3675497b6d219b5389ea56175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> choices from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5f75d5640511863d6a020f8f544fcf2ccd74fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|X\\cap Y| = (k-1)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6efc9c9acf954d93bf512e3e97c503b93b8450.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(k) = |\\Omega| - |X| - |Y| + |X\\cap Y| = (k+1)^4 - k^4 - k^4 + (k-1)^4 = 12k^2 + 2.\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Testing small values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we calculate\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/52209babe0e3b0ffeec3fb79b24122127f5a37d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1) = 14 = 2\\cdot 7, f(2) = 50 = 2\\cdot 5^2,  f(3) = 2\\cdot 5 \\cdot 11, \\dots\\]\" width=\"436\" height=\"20\" />\nWe can note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d879284367dcdab60fb2f20bf51b8b1694deaea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)f(2)f(3) = 77,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />, so at minimum, the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> can use the exponents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c13f88915d101b401e1fdeac1b195262655caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. To further minimize it, we assign larger exponents to smaller primes, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442faeecd0ddb0e23f4f8a8a28ef697ffc0246c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=2^3 3^2 5^1=360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474284d1d91941164bea639aea9cf16467a5c85d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=360 \\cdot 77 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}27,720}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"214\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Note: it can formally proven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0bc59fe3f7631564c5a8bc86b900dfefc3418dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)f(2)f(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> achieves the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/763fd7a7a20f70b951076258318f2af47926d61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k) = 12k^2 + 2 = 2(6k^2 + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/357cc51331aa8db31e02ecf8c8e5289135a1747f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6k^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is odd, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81232ecd8d9e4b5c0f24a00dabec238068f26de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> has exactly one factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e526e85e7c4a20e03bed8eebd8e4c962236e557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77,000 = 2^3 \\cdot 5^3 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must have exactly three prime factors, so only three <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81232ecd8d9e4b5c0f24a00dabec238068f26de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> are multiplied.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016